    "notes": "Three parts: Violin (small treble staff), Violoncello (small bass staff) and Piano (normal-size grand staff, ONE part). The violin and cello staves form a treble+bass pair joined by a BRACKET - they are two separate instruments and must NOT be merged into one two-staff part; the piano staves are joined by a BRACE and must NOT be split. Instrument names appear only on the first system. Menuetto (mm. 1-16, repeats, \"Fine\" after m.16), Trio (mm. 17-32, C major, repeats, \"Menuetto D.C. al Fine\" after m.32) - notated order, not unrolled."
  },
